# Host install and build output. The image runs `yarn install` and the web
# build itself; copying these from the host both inflates the context
# (node_modules alone is ~760 MB) and risks baking in artefacts for the
# wrong platform.
#
# `**` is required: a bare `node_modules` only matches at the context root.
# See https://docs.docker.com/build/concepts/context/#dockerignore-files
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/out
**/*.vsix

# Local tooling and indexes. None of these are read by
# `yarn workspace web build`.
#
# `.vscode-test` is a full VS Code download used only by the extension's
# integration tests. A bare `.vscode-test` would not match
# `packages/dbml-vs-code-extension/.vscode-test` (~1.2 GB) — that is what
# made `docker compose up --build` transfer a gigabyte of context.
.git
.github
.husky
.scratch
.claude
.codegraph
.superpowers
.yarn
.vscode
**/.vscode-test

# Workspace members the site does not compile against. Yarn still needs
# each package.json so `workspaces: ["packages/*"]` resolves; the Dockerfile
# copies those by name before `COPY . .`. Everything else in these trees
# stays out of the context.
packages/dbml-vs-code-extension/**
!packages/dbml-vs-code-extension/package.json
packages/db-to-dbml/**
!packages/db-to-dbml/package.json
packages/extension-shared/**
!packages/extension-shared/package.json
packages/schema-diff/**
!packages/schema-diff/package.json
# The MkDocs plugin is Python; its local environment (~80 MB) and the frame it
# vendors (~20 MB) would otherwise ride along in every image build.
packages/mkdocs-dbml/**
!packages/mkdocs-dbml/package.json

# Tests, coverage, docs, and editor noise.
docs
**/coverage
**/test-results
playwright-report
**/e2e
**/__tests__
**/tests
**/*.test.ts
**/*.test.tsx
**/*.spec.ts
**/*.spec.tsx
**/*.stories.ts
**/*.stories.tsx
**/*.log
**/.DS_Store
